{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q021_nad_binding_convergent_evolution","answer":"NAD(P) binding is a biochemical capability that has evolved in multiple structural lineages, not a marker of one universal homologous group. Its occurrence in different folds and superfamilies supports independent recruitment and convergent evolution of cofactor binding; within a homologous superfamily, diversification from a common ancestor represents divergent evolution. Different SCOPe assignments alone do not prove independent origins or exclude extremely remote ancestry.

For example, SCOPe 2.08 places NAD(P)-binding Rossmann-fold domains in superfamily c.2.1 (SUNID 51735), fold c.2, class c (α/β). The NAD-binding domain of HMG-CoA reductase belongs to family d.58.20.1, superfamily d.58.20 (SUNID 55035), ferredoxin-like fold d.58, class d (α+β). Thus NAD binding spans distinct structural frameworks. SCOPe families indicate clear evolutionary relationships; superfamilies unite families with evidence for probable common ancestry. A shared fold establishes structural similarity without necessarily establishing homology, and a shared class describes only broad secondary-structure organization.

The same cofactor imposes similar geometric and chemical constraints, so unrelated proteins can independently evolve similar phosphate-binding loops, hydrogen bonds, or catalytic residue arrangements. Short motifs and local active-site resemblance therefore cannot establish common ancestry. A convincing homology inference requires broader evidence such as statistically significant sequence/profile similarity across the domain, conserved structural topology and residue correspondence beyond the binding pocket, and compatible evolutionary relationships. Shared NAD(P) binding alone does not justify transferring substrate specificity, reaction mechanism, NAD versus NADP preference, or a whole-domain modeling template; those require appropriate sequence/structure comparisons and biochemical evidence.","evidence_used":["Pretrained biological knowledge","mcp__scope__get_scop_service_info","mcp__scope__search_scop","mcp__scope__get_scop_node","/api/v1/","/api/v1/releases/current","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=NAD&mode=auto&limit=15","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51735","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51735/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/55037","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/55037/parents"]}]}
